, market access and health economics, and outcomes research, as well as RWE services. Fortrea Holdings Inc. was incorporated in 2023 and is headquartered in Durham, North Carolina.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Anshul  Thakral | CEO & Director | Age 47 | Compensation: $1.7M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 14K people. Revenue per employee of $195K ranks in the bottom quartile among Healthcare peers, with revenue falling 6%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $6K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $5K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 9\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (6/10).","financial_summary":["Fortrea Holdings Inc. is a small-cap healthcare business with a $1.9B market cap on $2.7B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -6% over the past three years, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome. Operating margins are contracting by -17.0pp, the first warning that competitive pressure is eroding the franchise.","Returns on capital run at -6% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $88M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 3 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","On the balance sheet, thin -9.6\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Operating margins contracting -17.0pp YoY \u2014 competitive pressure is eroding the franchise","sev":"red","cat":"trend"},{"text":"Price sits 114% above esti